2025-12-09 05:00:02,021 [WARNING] translation: deep-translator error: Medline Seeks $5.37 Billion in This Year’s Biggest US IPO --> Text length need to be between 0 and 50 characters
2025-12-09 05:00:02,380 [INFO] translation: Translating article content...
2025-12-09 05:00:02,381 [WARNING] translation: deep-translator error: Medline Inc. offices in Waukegan, Illinois.

Listen

3:49

Medline Inc. is seeking to raise as much as $5.37 billion in a US initial public offering, setting the stage for what would be among the biggest-ever private equity backed listings.

The Northfield, Illinois-based company is marketing 179 million shares for $26 to $30 each, according to its filing Monday with the US Securities and Exchange Commission. The company, which counts Blackstone Inc. , Carlyle Group Inc. and Hellman & Friedman among its backers, has lined up $2.35 billion in commitments from so-called cornerstone investors.

The medical supplies maker and distributor would be valued at as much as $55.3 billion, according to the filing. Medline will easily deliver the largest IPO in the US this year if it prices within the marketed range, well above Venture Global Inc. ’s $1.75 billion offering in January. At the top of the price range it would raise $5.37 billion, making it the biggest in the world, surpassing Chinese battery maker Contemporary Amperex Technology Co. Ltd.’s $5.26 billion Hong Kong offering.

The deal would also easily top the $4.35 billion listing in 2011 of HCA Healthcare Inc. , which counted private equity firms KKR & Co. and Bain Capital among its backers.

The filing comes after a US government shutdown that disrupted IPO plans for numerous candidates, including Medline, which had been expected to go public as soon as in November. The company filed publicly during the dispute, which ended Nov. 12.

Medline had net income of $977 million on revenue of $20.6 billion for the nine months ending Sept. 27, compared with net income of $911 million on revenue of $18.7 billion a year earlier, according to a filing.

The company manufactures and distributes medical supplies such as gloves, gowns and exam tables used by hospitals and doctors. It was taken private by Blackstone, Carlyle and Hellman & Friedman in a $34 billion deal in 2021 that was one of the largest leveraged buyouts of all time. The company had filed confidentially Bloomberg Terminal for the listing with the US SEC last December, but tariff uncertainty delayed its plans to go public in the first half of this year.

The laundry list of cornerstone investors includes Baillie Gifford , Capital Group , Morgan Stanley ’s Counterpoint Global, Durable Capital Partners , Singaporean sovereign wealth fund GIC Pte , Janus Henderson Investors , Viking Global Investors and WCM Investment Management .

Read More: Shutdown Stalemate Brings US IPO Holdouts Off the Sidelines

Medline was founded by brothers Jon and Jim Mills in 1966. The Mills family, which remained Medline’s largest individual shareholder after the buyout, will have a 17.8% voting power after the IPO. Blackstone, Carlyle and Hellman & Friedman will own 18% voting rights respectively after the deal.

Members of the Mills family and their affiliates have indicated an interest in buying up to $250 million in shares at the IPO, the filing showed.

Since the private equity buyout, the company transitioned to new leadership under Jim Boyle, a 28-year company veteran and its first chief executive officer not related to the Mills family. Medline acquired Ecolab Inc. ’s surgical solutions business in 2024 for about $905 million and has invested $1.6 billion in capital expenditures within its distribution network in the past five years, the filing shows.

Medline has more than 43,000 employees worldwide, according to the filing.

Goldman Sachs Group Inc. , Morgan Stanley, Bank of America Corp. and JPMorgan Chase & Co. are working on the offering, along with 21 joint bookrunning managers and 21 co-managers. Medline expects to begin trading on the Nasdaq Global Select Market under the symbol MDLN.

(Updates with cornerstone investors in eighth paragraph.) --> Text length need to be between 0 and 50 characters
